[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711883556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103875#issuecomment-2711883556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103875","id":2711883556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hpA8k","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T21:28:26Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T21:28:26Z","body":"Thanks for the info about GNOME and Xfce, and the tooltip suggestion! If possible, I'd definitely like to keep the behavior consistent across platforms, so we don't need documentation that discerns between them. Do you know if <kbd>Meta</kbd> could work as a shortcut across all platforms, replacing <kbd>Alt</kbd>?\r\n\r\nI'd considered adding them with a dropdown similar to recovery mode, but it occurred to me that recovery mode and verbose mode aren't mutually exclusive, and further that if someone is opening a project in recovery mode, they might be more likely to also want the increased info that comes with verbose mode. As such, offering recovery mode and verbose mode as two distinct options wouldn't make sense.\r\n\r\nI suppose we could do the following:\r\n- Edit\r\n  - Edit in verbose mode\r\n  - Edit in recovery mode\r\n  - Edit in recovery + verbose mode\r\n\r\nWe might also be able to add a check box for verbose mode to the dialog box that shows up explaining recovery mode and confirming that the user wants to use it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711883556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711987939","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103875#issuecomment-2711987939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103875","id":2711987939,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hpabj","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T22:28:18Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T22:28:31Z","body":"> Do you know if Meta could work as a shortcut across all platforms, replacing Alt?\r\n\r\n<kbd>Meta</kbd> is the <kbd>Windows</kbd> key on Windows, so I wouldn't rely on it for anything in Godot. Pressing it will make the Start menu show up after all.\r\n\r\nOn macOS, it probably works fine, but regardless of the platform, I'd allow both modifiers just in case.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711987939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741868613","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103875#issuecomment-2741868613","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103875","id":2741868613,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jbZhF","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T23:19:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T23:19:29Z","body":"As much as I love the idea of holding down a key to swap the \"Edit\" button to \"Edit (Verbose)\", I'm thinking there might not be a good specific button to use. So far I've considered:\r\n- <kbd>Alt</kbd> - The original choice, but reserved by some OSs for window actions\r\n- <kbd>Meta</kbd> - Used by Windows for the Start Menu(?)\r\n- <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> - Would conflict with shortcuts like <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>E</kbd> for \"Edit Project\" (normally)\r\n- Because the project search bar is selected by default, other keys (letters, numbers, symbols) would type into that box\r\n\r\nAs such, it might make more sense just to have verbose mode be an option to select in the \"Edit\" dropdown. I've started working on that:\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2025-03-20 at 16 05 57@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c185298-70ca-4533-ae28-d024047d59b4)\r\n\r\nI'm not entirely sure if the \"recovery + verbose mode\" should be there. I don't know what icon would fit best for it, but if the others have icons, I definitely feel like it should too. (Honestly, maybe it'd make sense for recovery mode to include verbose mode automatically? Outside of this PR, of course.)\r\n\r\nTo go back to the original idea, perhaps we *could* add a keyboard shortcut like <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>E</kbd> for editing in verbose mode, and display it on the dropdown? It wouldn't have the neat button-text-switching effect that the original feature/PR proposes, but I think that's okay 😅\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741868613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741894018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103875#issuecomment-2741894018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103875","id":2741894018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jbfuC","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T23:43:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T23:43:13Z","body":"For now, the PR just has the \"Edit in verbose mode\" option under the dropdown menu, which launches the editor in verbose mode. The \"Edit in recovery + verbose mode\" option is gone, as is the ability to hold a key to change the \"Edit\" button to \"Edit (Verbose)\".\r\n\r\nFor now, since the details of the functionality are still being worked out, I'm not squashing the commits so that I can refer back to how I did certain things (like the hold-key thing) if we come up with a way it could work. If you'd prefer to squash them anyways, though, let me know and I can get that done 🙂 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741894018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745999078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103875#issuecomment-2745999078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repo